# Hau'oli Cemetery: the hillside of stones above the city, flowers on every grave and something small and pale watching
# from between them. A celesta in E minor, slow and a little hollow, over a harp's rocking arpeggio, a warm pad and a bell
# that tolls the root every other bar; no drums. The same by day and night, as the hill keeps its own hours.
# Original composition for this game, in the modern sound.
title Hau'oli Cemetery
tempo 66
meter 4/4
reverb 0.45
night none
room hall 2.8

